From c78f3a91e1246512849c97dde8a796149db6100c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cpu): vectorise the gated dsv4_hc_pre
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gated branch of ggml_compute_forward_dsv4_hc_pre_f32 ran one scalar
expf per element and stream. It now walks the thread's element range one
token segment at a time with row kernels: zero the segment, add
x*sigmoid(gate) for each stream with the new ggml_vec_mad_sigmoid_f32,
then scale. The thread split and the order of the sum over the streams
stay as they are.

The scalar loop still runs for the ungated branch, for use_ref, and when
x, the gate or dst has a non-contiguous first dimension.

The result is not bit-exact: the sigmoid uses ggml_v_expf, and the
compiler may contract a mul and add differently on either path. On the
test-backend-ops gated DSV4_HC_PRE cases the max abs error is 1.2e-07
and the NMSE is below 1.4e-14. The ungated cases stay bit-exact.

Depends on ggml_v_sigmoid from the previous commit. Ported from
ik_llama.cpp PR 2457 ("Simdify sigmoid evaluations"), which does the same
for its fused sigmoid-mul op.

